@startuml CryptoWeb-E3-mvc-wallettrading
title CryptoWeb - Wallet and Market Trade Settlement (MVC view)

!theme plain
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 75
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
hide circle


package "React views and API clients" {
  class "Trades" as TV <<React view>> {
    +Trades()
  }
  class "Wallet" as WV <<React view>> {
    +Wallet()
  }
  class "tradeApi" as TA <<API object>> {
    +getTradeHistory()
    +getUserHoldings()
    +cancelOrder()
  }
  class "walletApi" as WA <<API object>> {
    +getBalance()
  }
}

package "Controllers and collaborators" {
  class "Trade Controller (Server_3)" as STC <<controller module>> {
    +posttrade()
    +gettrades()
  }
  class "Core Gateway" as GW <<gateway module>> {
    +executeUserTrade()
  }
  class "Trade Controller (Core)" as CTC <<controller module>> {
    +execute()
  }
  class "Trade Service (Core)" as TS <<service module>> {
    +buy()
    +sell()
  }
  class "Wallet Controller (Core)" as WC <<controller module>> {
    +balance()
    +deposit()
    +withdraw()
  }
}

package "Data models" {
  class "Trade document" as MT <<Mongoose model>> {
    +referenceId
    +orderId
    +fillId
    +price
  }
  class "TradeFill record" as F <<MySQL entity>> {
    +id
    +status
    +wallet_tx_id
  }
  class "Wallet record" as W <<MySQL entity>> {
    +id
    +balance
    +status
  }
}

TV ..> TA
WV ..> WA
TA ..> STC : REST
WA ..> WC : Core REST
STC ..> GW
STC ..> MT : synchronize
GW ..> CTC : REST
CTC ..> TS
TS ..> F : SQL
TS ..> W : SQL
WC ..> W : SQL

legend bottom
The View and Model roles are identifiable; service modules remain part of the actual system.
endlegend

@enduml
